**REPORT BACK ON COMPLETION (mandatory, 3 steps — relay mode)**

When you finish your task (or hit a blocker), do these 3 things in order.
The orchestrator is hosted as a `codex app-server` (not interactive TUI),
so worker DONE reports go via a synchronous JSON-RPC relay instead of
Octogent channel-send.

### Step 1 — Display your full final report normally in chat

Write your COMPLETE final response as your normal assistant message in
this worker conversation. Status line first, then everything — branch,
commit, files, tests, blockers, follow-up. Readable Markdown.

### Step 2 — Mirror the same report to disk

Save the EXACT same content to a file in the project root. Name it
`reports/{{tid}}-<slug>.md` where `<slug>` is your task title from
`PROMPT N -- Title` converted to a filesystem-safe slug.

```bash
mkdir -p reports
cat > reports/{{tid}}-<your-task-slug>.md <<'REPORT_END'
# {{tid}} — <your task title verbatim>

[Same full content as your chat message — verbatim Markdown.]
REPORT_END
```

### Step 3 — Inject your DONE notification via the app-server relay

Pipe the single-line summary via stdin (shell-escape-safe):

```bash
cat > reports/{{tid}}-<your-task-slug>.summary.txt <<'SUMMARY_END'
DONE {{tid}}: {{n}}: TICKET-ID: STATUS // full report at reports/{{tid}}-<your-task-slug>.md
SUMMARY_END

"{{py_exe}}" -m gcs_orchestrator.relay "{{orch_sid}}" - < reports/{{tid}}-<your-task-slug>.summary.txt
RELAY_EXIT=$?
echo "relay exit code: $RELAY_EXIT"
```

**Relay exit codes:**
- `0` = success (orchestrator received + processed the turn)
- `2` = duplicate (you already sent this exact content; no-op, safe)
- `3` = lock timeout (>10 min queue contention; relay log at
  `%LOCALAPPDATA%\gcs-app-relay\relay.log` shows holder PID)
- `4` = app-server unreachable (your `reports/` file is durable backup)
- `5` = turn aborted/interrupted (orchestrator pressed Esc; don't auto-retry)
- `6` = turn timeout (>10 min; investigate manually)

For ANY non-zero exit, the file on disk is your durable record. Do NOT
spam retries; the relay has its own internal idempotency.

### What you should NOT do
- Do not skip Step 1 (chat display) — human-visible trail.
- Do not skip Step 2 (file on disk) — durable backup.
- Do not invent a Step 4 watchdog — the relay is synchronous + idempotent.
